From b84ab0d966b6378cefc13f1411bd587a056e1175 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aidan Coyne <raptros.v76@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:54:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Carry X11 clients' drags in Wayland drags

Satellite puts X windows on the X screen without knowing where the
compositor shows them, so an X client dragging looks for its XDND
target at a position that has nothing to do with the window under the
pointer: drops between X windows land on the wrong window or nowhere,
unless the windows happen to line up.

When an X client takes XdndSelection while a button is held on one of
our windows, satellite starts a Wayland drag from that window. The
compositor then says which surface the pointer is over:

- Over one of our X windows, Xwayland's pointer moves to the matching
  point on the X screen (relative to the window the drag started from,
  since entering another surface makes Xwayland release the button),
  and that window is raised, so the X client finds it and drives XDND
  with it itself.
- Over a Wayland client, an XdndAware proxy above every X window is the
  X client's target, and the Wayland client reads the data through
  XdndSelection conversions. Only "copy" is offered; DELETE and
  TIMESTAMP are not offered as types.

The drop ends with the button release the compositor kept. Windows of
type _NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE_DND get an empty input region, so drag icons
under the pointer don't become the drop target.
